      "text": "Lima"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:569e72e117968fcc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "9a5cd6a398f22821bf8d907506ba40c85854f306309d491bd837ba1f3435b966",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-0c9cd3aa-38d8-4e78-85c2-7fba7217988e",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, set out to explore the City of Kings. Your first stop is Love Park in Miraflores, home to The Kiss, a sculpture by Peruvian artist Víctor Delfín. The park opened on 14 February 1993. From the wall above the ocean, you can take in a sweeping view of the Pacific coast.\n\nContinue to Lima’s historic centre via San Isidro, where the city’s main financial institutions are based. On the main square stand the Government Palace, City Hall and the Archbishop’s Palace.\n\nLima Cathedral houses the tomb of Francisco Pizarro, the city’s founder. Cathedral admission is included. Then visit the Convent of Santo Domingo, with its narrow corridors. Admission is also included.\n\nFinish the day at the Larco Museum, which has a rich collection of goldwork and ceramics from Peru’s ancient cultures. After visiting the galleries, return to your hotel."
    },
